Explanation:
Save points are a sort of checkpoints that helps the user to roll back to their chosen save point in case of long transactions. The correct syntax for creating a savepoint is –
SAVEPOINT <savepoint_name>;
The save point name is user depended.

Question:
What will be the output of the following PL/SQL code?
